\ Neither collision key reaches the orphaned-method error. Both are turned off from the startup
\ file, and a redefinition that drops registered methods still throws.
\
\ The two collision kinds report a visibility surprise the program survives once the user accepts
\ it. This one reports methods going unreachable, which nothing later throws about, so a user who
\ relaxed it would never learn what they gave up.
use "testing" ;

"both keys off" test-section

\ Reading the values back is what makes the throw below evidence, rather than a startup file that
\ never arrived.
"dictionary-shadow" pragma-get "off" "the dictionary-shadow key is off" assert=
"import-collision" pragma-get "off" "the import-collision key is off" assert=

"the orphaned-method error is untouched" test-section

\ The redefinition has to share the generic's frame, so it runs at a loaded file's own top level.
[ "redef_drops_methods_conflict.1z" load ]
EOrphanedMethods "a redefinition dropping methods still throws" assert-error-type

"the guards the keys do reach stay silent" test-section

\ Both shadows land last: each one takes over its name for the rest of the file.
dup: ( -- x ) [ 0 ] ;
dup 0 "a native shadow is accepted and takes effect" assert=

use { taken: } "def_over_import_mod.1z" ;
taken: ( -- fixnum ) [ 1 ] ;
taken 1 "a definition over an import is accepted and takes effect" assert=
